    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d548">

                <pb facs="0752" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/9–1346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Protocol</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Woodward</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to Mr. Ben C. Limb,
                        Washington</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-23">September 23, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Receipt is acknowledged of your letter
                    dated September 13, 1946, together with its enclosures<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d548-f1"/> pertaining to your appointment as an official of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Representative Democratic Council of South
                    Korea</hi>.</p>
                <p>Your courtesy in making these documents available to the Department is
                    appreciated. Since it is understood, however, that the Council is acting as an
                    advisory body only to the United States Army Command in Korea, and therefore
                    local in character, there appears to be no basis upon which its recognition
                    abroad can be established.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanley Woodward</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
